# D3.js Data Loading (v6)

## Overview
D3.js provides built-in functions to load and parse various data formats including CSV, JSON, TSV, and more.

## Important: D3 v6 Changes
In D3 v6, data loading functions return Promises instead of using callbacks.

### Old way (D3 v5 and earlier):
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv", function(data) {
    // Process data
});
```

### New way (D3 v6+):
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv").then(function(data) {
    // Process data
});

// Or with async/await
async function loadData() {
    const data = await d3.csv("data.csv");
    // Process data
}
```

## Loading CSV Files

### Basic CSV Loading
```javascript
d3.csv("data/stocks.csv").then(data => {
    console.log(data);
    // data is an array of objects with column headers as keys
});
```

### CSV with Row Conversion
Parse and transform data as it loads:

```javascript
d3.csv("data/stocks.csv", d => {
    return {
        ticker: d.ticker,
        sector: d.sector,
        name: d["full name"],
        marketCap: +d.marketCap,  // Convert to number
        employees: +d.fullTimeEmployees,
        roe: +d.returnOnEquity
    };
}).then(data => {
    console.log(data);
});
```

**Note**: The `+` operator converts strings to numbers. Use it for all numeric fields.

### Handling Missing Values
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv", d => {
    return {
        ticker: d.ticker,
        marketCap: d.marketCap ? +d.marketCap : null,  // Handle empty values
        sector: d.sector || "Unknown"
    };
});
```

## Loading JSON Files

```javascript
d3.json("data/stocks.json").then(data => {
    console.log(data);
});
```

## Loading Multiple Files

Use `Promise.all()` to load multiple files:

```javascript
Promise.all([
    d3.csv("data/stocks.csv"),
    d3.json("data/metadata.json")
]).then(([stocks, metadata]) => {
    console.log("Stocks:", stocks);
    console.log("Metadata:", metadata);
    // Process combined data
});
```

## Auto-Type Conversion

D3 can automatically convert types:

```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv", d3.autoType).then(data => {
    // Numbers, dates, and booleans are automatically converted
});
```

## Common Data Formats

### CSV Format
```csv
ticker,sector,marketCap
AAPL,Technology,2676055080960
MSFT,Technology,2252284624896
```

### Loaded as:
```javascript
[
    { ticker: "AAPL", sector: "Technology", marketCap: "2676055080960" },
    { ticker: "MSFT", sector: "Technology", marketCap: "2252284624896" }
]
```

## Error Handling

```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv")
    .then(data => {
        console.log("Data loaded successfully");
    })
    .catch(error => {
        console.error("Error loading data:", error);
    });
```

## Other Loading Functions

```javascript
d3.text("file.txt")     // Load plain text
d3.xml("file.xml")      // Load XML
d3.tsv("file.tsv")      // Load TSV (tab-separated)
d3.dsv(";", "file.csv") // Custom delimiter
```

## Data Processing After Loading

### Filtering
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv").then(data => {
    const filtered = data.filter(d => d.sector === "Technology");
});
```

### Sorting
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv").then(data => {
    data.sort((a, b) => b.marketCap - a.marketCap);  // Descending
});
```

### Grouping
```javascript
d3.csv("data.csv").then(data => {
    const grouped = d3.group(data, d => d.sector);
    // Returns Map: { "Technology" => [...], "Finance" => [...] }
});
```

### Nesting (Creating Hierarchies)
```javascript
const nested = d3.rollup(
    data,
    v => v.length,           // Aggregation function
    d => d.sector,           // Group by sector
    d => d.country           // Then by country
);
```

## Practical Example: Loading Stock Data

```javascript
async function initialize() {
    try {
        // Load stock descriptions
        const stocks = await d3.csv("data/stock-descriptions.csv", d => ({
            ticker: d.ticker,
            sector: d.sector,
            name: d["full name"],
            marketCap: d.marketCap ? +d.marketCap : null,
            employees: d.fullTimeEmployees ? +d.fullTimeEmployees : null,
            country: d.country,
            website: d.website
        }));

        // Filter out items without required data
        const validStocks = stocks.filter(d => d.ticker && d.sector);

        // Create visualization
        createVisualization(validStocks);

    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Failed to load data:", error);
    }
}

initialize();
```

## Relative vs Absolute Paths

```javascript
// Relative to HTML file location
d3.csv("data/file.csv")           // Works if data folder is in same directory
d3.csv("./data/file.csv")         // Explicit relative path
