Adjust legend position based on available space:

```javascript
function createLegend(svg, colorScale, width, height) {
    const legendData = colorScale.domain();

    // Determine position based on chart size
    let legendX, legendY;
    if (width > 800) {
        // Place on right side for wide charts
        legendX = width - 180;
        legendY = 30;
    } else {
        // Place on bottom for narrow charts
        legendX = 20;
        legendY = height + 40;
    }

    const legend = svg.append("g")
        .attr("class", "legend")
        .attr("transform", `translate(${legendX}, ${legendY})`);

    // ... add legend items
}
```

## Complete Example

```javascript
function createColorLegend(svg, colorScale, x, y) {
    const legend = svg.append("g")
        .attr("class", "color-legend")
        .attr("transform", `translate(${x}, ${y})`);

    // Title
    legend.append("text")
        .attr("class", "legend-title")
        .attr("x", 0)
        .attr("y", -10)
        .text("Sector")
        .style("font-size", "14px")
        .style("font-weight", "bold")
        .style("fill", "#333");

    const legendData = colorScale.domain();

    // Background
    const bgHeight = legendData.length * 28 + 10;
    legend.append("rect")
        .attr("x", -10)
        .attr("y", -30)
        .attr("width", 170)
        .attr("height", bgHeight + 20)
        .attr("fill", "white")
        .attr("stroke", "#ddd")
        .attr("rx", 4);

    // Items
    const items = legend.selectAll(".legend-item")
        .data(legendData)
        .join("g")
        .attr("class", "legend-item")
        .attr("transform", (d, i) => `translate(0, ${i * 28})`)
        .style("cursor", "pointer");

    items.append("circle")
        .attr("cx", 9)
        .attr("cy", 0)
        .attr("r", 8)
        .attr("fill", d => colorScale(d))
        .attr("stroke", "#666")
        .attr("stroke-width", 1);

    items.append("text")
        .attr("x", 24)
        .attr("y", 0)
        .attr("dy", "0.35em")
        .text(d => d)
        .style("font-size", "13px")
        .style("font-family", "Arial, sans-serif")
        .style("fill", "#333");

    return legend;
}

// Usage
const legend = createColorLegend(svg, colorScale, width - 200, 40);
```

## Best Practices

1. **Position thoughtfully** - Don't overlap with data
2. **Keep it simple** - Only include necessary information
3. **Use consistent styling** - Match chart's visual design
4. **Make it readable** - Sufficient contrast and font size
5. **Consider mobile** - Legend might need to move for small screens
6. **Add interactivity** - Let users filter/highlight data
7. **Order logically** - Alphabetical or by frequency

## Resources
- [D3 Observable: Color Legend](https://observablehq.com/@d3/color-legend)
- [Susie Lu's d3-legend library](https://d3-legend.susielu.com/)

